  Slug: otherworldly-protection
  DisplayName: Otherworldly Protection
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/features/classes/otherworldly-protection.webp
  Description: Just because you prefer science doesn't mean you can't build your
    armor with materials and gizmos designed to protect against otherworldly attacks.
    You gain resistance equal to 3 + half your level to void damage, or to vitality
    damage if you have void healing (such as if you're a dhampir). You gain the same
    amount of resistance to spirit damage. If you are sanctified (such as by also
    being a champion or cleric dedicated to a deity who allows or enforces sanctification)
    this resistance applies to unholy damage (if you are sanctified holy) or holy
    damage (if you are sanctified unholy), regardless of what other traits the damage
    has.
  SourceTitle: Pathfinder Guns & Gears
  SourcePack: classfeatures
  Rarity: common
